                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{d} \;\colon\; \Omega^\bullet(J^\infty_\Sigma(E)) \longrightarrow \Omega^{\bullet+1}(J^\infty_\Sigma(E))
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since the jet bundle unified spacetime with field values, we want to decompose this differential into a contribution coming from forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+derivatives"} total derivatives
              of fields along spacetime (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+derivatives"}> horizontal derivatives
              ”), and actual
              %em variation
              of fields at a fixed spacetime point (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+derivatives"}> vertical derivatives
              ”):
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+derivative"} total spacetime derivative
              or
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+derivative"} horizontal derivative
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi J
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^\infty_\Sigma(E)
