                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^{(\Delta^1)}
          %p
            This subtle interplay of “bulk fields” and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT+with+defects"}> defect fields
            ” which is here captured most naturally in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            cannot really be expressed accurately just in terms of field bundles.
          %h4#HigherGaugeFields Higher gauge fields
          %p
            Above we have seen the generalization of field bundles to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            already for traditional notions such as Yang-Mills fields and Spin-structures. But many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theories
            considered in theoretical physics have fields that are more “explicitly” entities in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
          %p
            For instance the higher analog of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            which is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kalb-Ramond+field"} Kalb-Ramond field
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} 2-connection
            on a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            %a{:href => "magnetic+charge#MagneticChargeAnomaly"} magnetic charge anomaly
            (as discussed there) has no accurate description in terms of field bundles. Next the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} 3-connection
            on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+3-bundle"} principal 3-bundle
          %p
            There is a wide variety of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theories"} higher dimensional Chern-Simons theories
            whose fields are such
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
            applied to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundles"} field bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton+sectors"} instanton sectors
            and pretending that a field configuration for these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} ∞-connections
            are given by globally defined
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolumes"} worldvolumes
            of very special topology or low
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
