          %h3#RelationOfFieldsToSections
            Relation to sections of fiber
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We discuss here how def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FieldsInAnActionFunctional"}
            equivalently says that fields are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} fiber ∞-bundle
            which is which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} associated
            to a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"}> principal
            )
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"} background field
          %p
            For simplicity of the discussion first consider the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi BgFields
                  %mo ≃
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{BgFields} \simeq \mathbf{B}G
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in Grp(\mathbf{H})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            we instead have the differential refinement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            (see below at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#GaugeFields"} Examples – Gauge fields
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#BriefReviewOfPrincipalInfinityBundlesAsBackgroundFields"} Background fields as principal ∞-bundles
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#FieldsAsSectionsOfAssociatedBundles"} Fields as sections of associated fiber ∞-bundles
          %h4#BriefReviewOfPrincipalInfinityBundlesAsBackgroundFields
            Background fields as principal
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We briefly recall the central aspects of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon * \to \X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"}> (∞,1)-pullback
            ) of the point along itse is the based
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi x
                  %mi X
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega_x X  \coloneqq \{x\} \underset{X}{\times} \{x\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Via composition of loops, this canonically has the structure of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} A-∞ algebra
            object such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} 0-truncation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi x
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_0 \Omega_x X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
            which is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            %em
              groupal
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            are
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} group objects
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
