          %h3#SigmaModelFields
            %strong 0)
            Sigma-model fields
          %p
            Traditionally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            field is a type of fields given simply by (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"}> smooth
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to X
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FieldsInAnActionFunctional"}
            and as shown in the following sections, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            %em every
            type of field is of this form if we allow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be a general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            and functions to be maps in a suitable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            fields also in the traditional restrictive sense of the term.
          %h4#UnchargedScalarField Uncharged scalar field
          %p
            A
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
            is given simply by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            on
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            (“real scalar field”) or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            (“complex scalar field”). Hence this is the example of def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FieldsInAnActionFunctional"}
            with trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+fields"} background fields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi BgFields
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{BgFields} \coloneqq *
          %p
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Fields} \;\colon\; \mathbb{R} \to *
          %p
            from (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            underlying) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            to the point, or else
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Fields} \;\colon\; \mathbb{C} \to *
          %p
            regarded as an object in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
