            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            and its variants, as shown by the following examples.
          %p For recognizing traditional constructions in this formulation, the following basic fact is important.
          #CosetIsHomotopyFiberOfDeloopedInclusion.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_13 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi H
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \colon H \hookrightarrow G
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
              inclusion of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi H
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi ι
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G/H \to \mathbf{B}H \stackrel{\mathbf{B}\iota}{\to} \mathbf{B}G
            %p
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
              on the left.
          %h5#OrdinaryGravity Gravity
          %p
            We discuss the formulation of the field of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            as a special case of def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FieldsInAnActionFunctional"}
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_12 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
