          %p
            are one component of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
          %h3#MatterFields
            %strong II)
            Matter fields
          %p
            Fundamental
            = succeed "-fields" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter"} matter
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutrinos"} neutrinos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/force"} force
            fields that interact with the matter fields and where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            underlying such a force
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            %em
              %a{:href => "#GaugeFields"} Gauge fields
            above, and, if we are talking indeed about fermions, to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+bundle"} spin bundle
            given by the gravity-spin structure field discussed in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#MatterFields"} Gravity and generalized geometry
            above.
          %p
            More precisely, fermioninc matter fields are sections of these bundles regarded in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            with the fibers regarded as odd-graded. (…)
          %h4#SectionsOfAssociatedBundles
            %strong General
            – sections of associated fiber
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We start by discussing the general mechanism by which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of
            = succeed "-" do
