          %h2#references References
          %h3#lecture_notes_and_expositions Lecture notes and expositions
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} geometry of physics – perturbative quantum field theory
              , chaper
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+perturbative+quantum+field+theory#Fields"} 3. Fields
          %p A survey of the main field species is given in
          %ul
            %li#Kocic16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikica+Kocic"}> Mikica Kocic
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Overview of the fields in QFT
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/FieldSpecies.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Most of the above material as of 2013 was written as part of a lecture series
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher Chern-Simons theory
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www2.ims.nus.edu.sg/Programs/013wquantum/index.php"} Workshop on Topological Aspects of Quantum Field Theories, Singapore (14 - 18 Jan 2013)
              on the first sections at
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry%20of%20physics#PHYSICS"} geometry of physics, II) Physics
          %p A exposition specifically for gauge fields is also in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.physicsforums.com/insights/examples-prequantum-field-theories-gauge-fields/"} Examples for Prequantum field theories I: Gauge fields
          %p
            An exposition of the general formulation of fields in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} slice (∞,1)-toposes
            is in section 4 of
          %ul#FiorenzaSatiSchreiberCSIntroAndSurvey
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/A+higher+stacky+perspective+on+Chern-Simons+theory"} A higher stacky perspective on Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            Lecture notes on fields as discussed here with applications in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            are in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+smooth+cohomology+in+string+theory"} twisted smooth cohomology in string theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://maths-old.anu.edu.au/esi/2012/"} K-theory and Quantum Fields
          %p An introductory survey is also in section 1 of
          %ul#dcct
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %h3#original_articles_on_the_general_notion Original articles on the general notion
          %p
            For references on the tradtional formulation of physical fields by sections of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundles"} field bundles
            as discussed
            %a{:href => "#IdeaOfFieldBundlesAndItsProblems"} above
            see there references
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} there
          %p
            The formulation of physical fields as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            as in the
            = succeed "-section" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Definition"} Definition
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Background+fields+in+twisted+differential+nonabelian+cohomology"} Background fields in twisted differential nonabelian cohomology
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oberwolfach+Workshop%2C+June+2009+--+Strings%2C+Fields%2C+Topology"} Oberwolfach Workshop, June 2009 – Strings, Fields, Topology
          %p Further articles since then are listed at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p
            In particular the general notion of fields as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+c-structures"} twisted differential c-structures
            appears in
          %ul#SSS
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Twisted+Differential+String+and+Fivebrane+Structures"} Twisted Differential String and Fivebrane Structures
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4001"}> arXiv:0910.4001
              )
          %p
            and the general theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+coefficient+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} local coefficient ∞-bundles
            as referred to in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#RelationToTwistedCohomology"} Relation to twisted cohomology
            above as well as the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} associated ∞-bundles
            as in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#SectionsOfAssociatedBundles"} Sections of associated ∞-bundles
            is laid out in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles+--+theory%2C+presentations+and+applications"} Principal ∞-bundles – theory, presentations and applications
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0248"}> arXiv:1207.0248
              )
          %p Some examples of fields in this sense are called “relative fields” in
          %ul#FreedTeleman
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em Relative quantum field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1212.1692"}> arXiv:1212.1692
              )
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} AQFT
            with stacky fields and co-stacky
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+nets+of+observables"} local nets of observables
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BeniniSchenkelSzabo15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Benini"}> Marco Benini
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Schenkel"} Alexander Schenkel
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
              %em Homotopy colimits and global observables in Abelian gauge theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1503.08839"}> arXiv:1503.08839
              )
          %h3#original_articles_on_special_cases Original articles on special cases
          %p
            The supergeometric nature of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            had been pointed out in
          %ul#Precis
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"}> Jacques Distler
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
              %em Orientifold Précis
              in:
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              (eds.)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
              Proceedings of Symposia in Pure Mathematics, AMS (2011) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0906.0795"}> arXiv:0906.0795
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/bilbao.pdf"} slides
          %p with a more detailed account in
          %ul#FreedLectures
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              %em Lectures on twisted K-theory and orientifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/ESI.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The formulation of this in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+infinity-groupoids"} smooth super infinity-groupoids
            is (
            %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSatiSchreiberCSIntroAndSurvey"}> FSS, section 4.3
            ).
